vidvān yuktaḥ samācaran\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":1146,\"bb\":1020,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/3/26/b1020/\",\"shadow_value\":\"na – not; buddhi-bhedam – disruption of intelligence; janayet – he should cause; ajñānām – of the foolish; karma-saṅginām – who are attached to fruitive work; joṣayet – he should dovetail; sarva – all; karmāṇi – work; vidvān – a learned person; yuktaḥ – engaged; samācaran – practicing.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"not\"},{\"word\":\"buddhi-bhedam\",\"translation\":\"disruption of intelligence\"},{\"word\":\"janayet\",\"translation\":\"he should cause\"},{\"word\":\"ajñānām\",\"translation\":\"of the foolish\"},{\"word\":\"karma-saṅginām\",\"translation\":\"who are attached to fruitive work\"},{\"word\":\"joṣayet\",\"translation\":\"he should dovetail\"},{\"word\":\"sarva\",\"translation\":\"all\"},{\"word\":\"karmāṇi\",\"translation\":\"work\"},{\"word\":\"vidvān\",\"translation\":\"a learned person\"},{\"word\":\"yuktaḥ\",\"translation\":\"engaged\"},{\"word\":\"samācaran\",\"translation\":\"practicing\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":1147,\"bb\":1021,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/3/26/b1021/\",\"body_value\":\"So as not to disrupt the minds of ignorant men attached to the fruitive results of prescribed duties, a learned person should not induce them to stop work. Rather, by working in the spirit of devotion, he should engage them in all sorts of activities [for the gradual development of Kṛṣṇa consciousness].\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1148,\"bb\":1022,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/3/26/b1022/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 3.